<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Equation of the locus at a distance from a point</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Write an equation for the locus of points \({@r@}\) units from \(C({@a@}, {@b@})\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The locus of a point \(P\) is \({@eqb@}\). Give the centre and the radius of the circle, the radius correct to 1 decimal place where it is not a whole number.</p><div>Centre \(\big(\)[[input:ans2]], [[input:ans3]]\(\big)\) [[validation:ans2]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>Radius [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) By Pythagoras, the distance from \(P(x, y)\) to \(C({@a@}, {@b@})\) is \(\sqrt{(x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2}\) with \(a = {@a@}\) and \(b = {@b@}\). Setting it equal to \({@r@}\) and squaring both sides gives</p><p>\[{@tas@}\]</p><p>Any equivalent equation is accepted, for example the expanded form.</p><p>(b) In \((x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2\) the centre is \((h, k)\) and the right-hand side is the square of the radius. So the centre is \(({@c@}, {@dd@})\) and the radius is [[if test="integerp(rk)"]]\(\sqrt{{@k@}} = {@rk@}\)[[else]]\(\sqrt{{@k@}} \approx {@dispdp(float(floor(10^1*(rk)+1/2)/10^1),1)@}\)[[/if]].</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: equation of a circle from its centre and radius, and back. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, Chapter 7, A9 and A10. */
a: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0]);
b: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0,a,-a]);
/* bn: excluded circles [centre x, centre y, r^2]: those in this chapter (examples, exercises, the how-to-type line) and in the source textbook. Part (a) never gives one of them, part (b) never prints one. */
bn: [[0,0,169],[0,0,49],[2,1,25],[5,-2,16],[-4,7,36],[1,-2,4],[6,3,16],[-2,0,25],[1,-6,9],[-2,-2,49],[2,6,16],[-3,4,25],[4,0,7],[-2,-3,25],[3,-5,194],[-4,-2,10],[1,4,9],[2,1,4],[1,-3,9],[-5,2,11],[0,5,49],[-4,3,36],[0,3,9],[2,6,40],[8,1,50],[6,0,16],[-3,2,13],[2,3,50],[3,3,4],[-2,1,20],[-3,1,117],[-1,3,10],[1,8,16],[4,2,17],[2,1,100],[0,2,10],[3,0,9],[0,0,6],[4,2,5],[3,2,9],[-2,-1,17],[4,4,10],[-2,0,12],[3,1,10],[1,2,1],[5,-1,50],[-4,-1,8],[1,0,10],[0,1,85],[4,1,4],[-2,-3,9],[1,-7,49],[1,-7,7],[2,1,36],[0,-3,25],[-2,-4,3],[-1,-2,13],[-2,7,49],[4,1,8],[-2,4,100],[1,-3,289],[4,5,25],[4,-5,36],[3,-1,49],[15,0,81],[0,0,144],[-5,2,16],[1,-4,9],[-3,5,16],[2,-1,100]];
exr: map(lambda([t], sqrt(t[3])), sublist(bn, lambda([t], is(t[1]=a) and is(t[2]=b))));
r: rand_with_prohib(2,9,exr);
ta1: (x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r^2;
/* diagnostics: radius not squared; signs of the centre kept; coordinates swapped */
dr: (x-a)^2+(y-b)^2=r;
ds: (x+a)^2+(y+b)^2=r^2;
dsw: (x-b)^2+(y-a)^2=r^2;
sg(v) := if is(v<0) then sconcat("+",-v) else sconcat("-",v);
tas: sconcat("(x",sg(a),")^2+(y",sg(b),")^2=",r^2);
c: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0]);
dd: rand_with_prohib(-6,6,[0,c,-c]);
k: rand(sublist([3,5,7,10,12,13,16,20,25,29,34,36,40,45,49], lambda([z], not member([c,dd,z], bn))));
rk: sqrt(k);
eqb: sconcat("(x",sg(c),")^2+(y",sg(dd),")^2=",k);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
