  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Loci: equation of a circle locus</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.3: Write the equation of the locus of points a fixed distance from a point, and read the centre and radius from such an equation.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 7, Section A, questions A9 and A10 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: equation from centre and radius and back, framed as a locus; new random centres and radii, with C1's own excluded.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
