    <node><name>3</name><description>Coordinates swapped</description><answertest>AlgEquiv</answertest><sans>ans1</sans><tans>dsw</tans><testoptions></testoptions><quiet>0</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-4-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Your equation is the locus of points \({@r@}\) units from \(({@b@}, {@a@})\), not from \(C({@a@}, {@b@})\). The \(x\)-coordinate of \(C\) goes in the bracket with \(x\) and the \(y\)-coordinate in the bracket with \(y\).</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>4</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-4-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
    <node><name>4</name><description>Correct equation with the square root kept</description><answertest>AlgEquiv</answertest><sans>ans1</sans><tans>sqrt((x-a)^2+(y-b)^2)=r</tans><testoptions></testoptions><quiet>0</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>1.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-5-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Squaring both sides gives the usual form \({@tas@}\).</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>-1</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-5-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="tst"]]Test your equation with a point that must be on the locus: \(({@tp0[1]@}, {@tp0[2]@})\) is \({@r@}\) units from \(C({@a@}, {@b@})\), straight across or straight up or down from it. At that point your left-hand side is \({@lv0@}\) and your right-hand side is \({@rv0@}\), so the point is not on your locus. Write the distance from \((x, y)\) to \(C\) by Pythagoras and set it equal to \({@r@}\).[[else]]By Pythagoras the distance from \((x, y)\) to \((a, b)\) is \(\sqrt{(x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2}\). Set it equal to the distance and square both sides.[[/if]]</p>]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
